extraction_notes: "WB13 Lone Star printed 81-83 (cache p082-p084, cache page = printed folio + 1): the introduction is at the foot of printed 81, the stat block and skills on 82, penalties, equipment and money on 83. Every number was read off 170 dpi renders of cache p083 and p084. The Monkey Boy Soldier R.C.C. that starts on printed 83 is another class. Imported as a playable class on Nate''s instruction; the book''s Player Character Note and the Experience Tables note on printed 174 are restriction lines. || HEADING: Mini Monkey Spies R.C.C., under Monkey Boys in the mutant animal chapter: a race. It states sdc_base, so no men_of_arms line is carried. || XP: the ladder headed Monkey Mini Spy & Most Intelligent Mutant Animals on the unnumbered page after printed 174 (cache p176), lower bound of each band: 0, 1801, 2601, 5201, 15001, 25001, 35001, 45001, 75001, 95001, 150001, 200001, 250001, 300001, 350001. || ATTRIBUTES as printed 82: Average I.Q. 7 (a fixed number, stored as the fixed value 7), M.E. 3D6, M.A. 3D6, P.S. 1D6+4, P.P. 3D6+6, P.E. 2D6+8, P.B. 3D6, Spd 2D6+10 running (double in trees, a natural ability). || POOLS: Hit Points P.E. plus 1D4 per level. S.D.C. is printed as P.E. attribute number +3D6 with no ''plus those gained from skills'' wording, a complete figure, so it is stored as sdc_base (the Ursa-Warrior reading in this book), not as a pool bonus. The larger-species figures (bonus hit points of 1D6 or 2D6, S.D.C. +5D6) are not stored: the book gives no rule for who is a larger species. P.P.E. 4D6. Magic none, psionics none. || COMBAT: attacks per round 2 to start, +1 at levels 3, 6, 9 and 13, stored as attacks_base 2 and four at_level entries. Hand to Hand: Not applicable, stored as hand_to_hand costs {} (no style granted, none offered). +2 initiative and +4 roll with fall or impact are unconditional. Dodge is printed +2 on the ground or +4 in trees: +2 is stored, the figure that always applies, and the tree figure is text in the Combat ability. || NATURAL ABILITIES: Swim 30%, Climb 95%/90% and Prowl 56% +2% per level are stored as the catalog skills Swimming (30, no per-level gain printed), Climbing (95, none printed) and Prowl (56, per_level 2), and restated as text. Acrobatics 90% is text only (judgement): the catalog Acrobatics skill carries attribute and roll bonuses that the book does not give this animal, whose own roll bonus is printed separately. Identify edible plants 80% is text; it is not the Identify Plants & Fruit skill, which the related list sells separately at +10%. || R.C.C. SKILLS (printed 82): American at 80% is Language: Native Tongue 80, per_level 0. Radio: Basic 45+10 = 55. Optic Systems 30+5 = 35. TV/Video (basic, no bonus) is T.V./Video 25. Surveillance Systems (and Tailing, not tracking; +5%) is the two catalog skills Surveillance 30+5 = 35 and Tailing 30+5 = 35. Pick Pockets 25+5 = 30. Land Navigation 36+20 = 56. Wilderness Survival 30+15 = 45. W.P. Knife. || RELATED: three at level one, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. Communications any. Domestic any -5. Electrical none. Espionage any +5 except sniper, forgery, tracking (Tracking (people)) and intelligence. Mechanical none. Medical First Aid only. Military Camouflage only +5. Physical Swim only. Pilot, Pilot Related none. Rogue any except computer hacking and card shark (Cardsharp). Science none. Technical: Art -5, language -10 and photography only, stored as three Technical entries so each keeps its own printed figure; language is every catalog skill whose name starts with Language. W.P. blunt, paired weapons and pistol only; ''pistol'' is stored as the three pistol proficiencies, Revolver, Automatic Pistol and Energy Pistol (judgement). Wilderness: identify plants +10 (Identify Plants & Fruit) and track animals -5 (Track & Trap Animals, the only animal-tracking skill in the catalog) only, as two entries. || SECONDARY: one at each of levels 1, 2, 4, 8, 10, 12 and 14, from the same list without the bonuses or penalties in parentheses. || EQUIPMENT (printed 83): light armor (11 M.D.C.) is custom made and matches no other catalog armor; the 11 M.D.C. custom light armor is its own gear row, mini-monkey-light-armor. S.D.C. scalpel is scalpel; laser scalpel is laser-scalpel; two flares; small binoculars is binoculars; small radio is walkie-talkie; pen flashlight, pocket mirror, small canteen is canteen, small backpack is backpack, utility belt, air filter. The printed comb is not stored: it has no catalog row and is a trivial personal item. Equipment available upon assignment is a restriction line, not granted. || MONEY: the book prints no salary and no starting credits, only that the CS provides for all the animal''s needs. No starting_money is stored; the line is a restriction. || OPTIONAL DOG BOY TABLES: the entry (printed 81-83) says nothing about the optional size, breed or mutation abnormality tables. Its only pointers to the Dog Boy are the riot control armor style and the dual I.D. system, restated from printed 35-36. The restriction line records that silence. || Penalties and Other Considerations are restriction lines in full. The population figures in the closing Note (Lone Star, Chi-Town, Tolkeen, Free Quebec) are lore."
