## Lore

Lone Star''s geneticists did not only build soldiers. One of their quieter
projects takes squirrel-sized monkeys and raises nothing but their minds, to
about the level of a slow human, leaving the body, the tail, the grip and the
instincts exactly as nature made them. The result is a Mini: a clever, obedient
little animal that can go where no person or Dog Boy can.

A Mini climbs drain pipes and brickwork, crosses wires, slips through a
half-open window or an air duct, and sits unnoticed above a street for hours.
It can work a point-and-click camera, plant a bug, tail a mark across the
rooftops and lift something small out of a pocket. It understands far more
speech than it can produce, managing only a handful of squeaked words. In
forest and jungle it scouts ahead; in a city full of tall buildings it is in
its element.

It is no fighter. A Mini is a plant eater a few pounds in weight, and anything
that hunts, from a house cat upward, is a danger to it once it is caught on
open ground.

## GM Notes

The book itself suggests this animal works better as an NPC than as a player
character, and its experience table is the one shared by the most intelligent
mutant animals. It has no hand to hand style and its attacks per round come
from its own table. Guns are nearly useless to it (-5 to strike, no bonuses);
its real weapons are a scalpel, a laser scalpel, thrown grenades and staying
out of reach. Remember the tree figures the sheet does not add: double speed
and +4 to dodge off the ground, and the 20% and 30% penalties for full
environmental armor and for snow and ice. A Mini outside Coalition service is
a runaway or the child of one, and is killed if the Coalition comes across it.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'mini-monkey-spy');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
